a maximum-two symbolic reduction axis carries a product iterator: true
its bound lowering emits the gh-490 extent guard: true
the guarded reduction of 37.0 over an extent-0 axis is the empty sum 0.0: true
an ordinary %op reduction reaches Accum_op with a maximum-one extent and no iterator: true
its product space is empty, so no loop exists for an extent guard to sit in: true
both sides of the reduction are indexed at element zero: true
zero is a legal runtime binding for a maximum-one extent: true
Accum_op lowering refuses a bound maximum-one symbolic extent: true
the refusal names Accum_op, the absent iterator and the element-zero write: true
the user-facing compile path refuses it too: true
the same extent left unbound still lowers, retaining maximum-shape semantics: true
that lowering is what the bound path emitted: it contains no guard for static indices to fill: true
the harness refuses every ~launch that does not value the parameter exactly once: true
the refused program would have returned its operand where the empty sum is 0.0: true
so the refusal guards a wrong VALUE in a concrete output cell, not a beyond-extent margin: true
